  "notes": "Raspy rock-and-disco pop, modelled on the defining 2020— mode. The drums are the entry's stated negative space: \"understated played kit with fizzy cymbals and a soft backbeat; the groove is carried by bass and guitar rather than by drum density\", so `fillDensity` and the perc density stay low, the snare transient is soft and the humanize block is a played one; the `ride` and `crash` lanes are the fizzy cymbals. The bass is the hook and the research says so outright — \"a funk bassline as the primary hook instrument (documented on Flowers), moving in syncopated 8ths and 16ths against a plain kick\" — so the kick sits square on 1 and 3 at a low syncopation while the bassline is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.3 with the widest passing-tone set and the highest `anticipationProb` in this batch. No `bass808` block: the entry says \"no 808\". Harmony is \"major-mode with 7th and 9th colour in the yacht-rock/disco mode\" over Rhodes and Wurlitzer, which is the extension spread. Melody \"sits low and conversational in verses and opens into a rasped sustained chorus; melodic cells repeat with lyric variation\" — a low register, `twoBarCellRepeat` and `endVariation`. The counter is the documented \"swooning string line (arranged for violin and viola)\", which is `sustain_pad` first. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because \"tempo/key bands inferred\"; every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the key/scale weighting and `bpm.mode` 110 (the midpoint of the first-named 95—125 disco-funk band) are INFERRED, and the entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the contralto placement claim is repeated here.",
